% ============================================================
% trialstyle.sty
% Style for "Pancreatic Cancer LLM Clinical Trial System: From IND to Protocol
% to Legislation, Funding, and AI Peer Review".  Draft 1.0, repository v4.6.0,
% San Diego, August 14, 2026.  FINAL stage (stage 8 of 8).
%
% STAGE 8 CHANGES TO THIS FILE.  Four, and nothing else:
%   i)   \figslot is retained and never called: every one of the paper's
%        twenty-five figures is drawn.  It stays defined so a figure can be
%        temporarily reverted to a placeholder without a style edit.
%   ii)  \seqrow and \ganttrow, carried from stage 7, are unchanged.
%   iii) \needspace before an inline figure now reserves the figure plus FOUR
%        lines rather than five.  Stage 7 measured every drawn figure and found
%        the five-line reserve pushing three figures to a fresh page and leaving
%        the preceding page a third empty; four lines is enough to keep a figure
%        with the paragraph that introduces it and no more.
%   iv)  \topfraction is raised from 0.86 to 0.90 and \floatpagefraction from
%        0.45 to 0.50, for the same reason: the drawn figures have a known
%        median height of 8.4cm and the stage 7 compile stranded space above
%        four of them.
%
% NOTHING ELSE MOVES.  In particular the spacing invariant is unchanged: appfig
% and apptable still close with a rigid \vskip 24.5pt, \figcaption and \tabcap
% still open with \nointerlineskip, and the source order
%     \end{appfig}  \vspace{-0.6cm}  \figcaption{...}
% still leaves exactly 7.44pt from the frame rule to the first caption line, for
% every one of the twenty-five figures and every one of the twenty-five tables,
% floating or inline, whatever precedes or follows it on the page.
%
% WHAT THIS STYLE IS.  It adapts capstyle.sty from
% funding/capitalization-plan/final-capital/publication and keeps that work's
% five TikZ diagram vocabularies, one per machine-readable diagram platform:
%
%   1) mermaid-type            (mm* styles)   flowchart / sequence / state / gantt
%   2) plantuml-type           (uml* styles)  use case / state with guards / activity
%   3) d2-type                 (d2* styles)   containers, grids, sql tables, layers
%   4) diagrams (python)-type  (dg* styles)   clustered infrastructure with glyphs
%   5) graphviz-type           (gv* styles)   dot records, clusters, fault trees
%
% WHAT IS NEW HERE.  Four things, and nothing else:
%
%   a) THE PALETTE IS BURGUNDY, NOT CORPORATE BLUE.  Burgundy #800020, Charcoal
%      #2E2E2E, Slate Gray #6B6B6B and Mist Gray #C9C9C9, plus two lighter
%      shades of Burgundy: #A32A3C and #E2D6D9.  Neither lighter shade reads as
%      pink, because the first keeps the saturation of the parent and only
%      raises its lightness, and the second is a warm mauve-gray obtained by
%      carrying Burgundy toward Mist Gray rather than toward white.  Charcoal is
%      a stroke and a text color ONLY: the master prompt forbids black filled
%      boxes, and a #2E2E2E fill would read as one, so no fill token in this
%      file is darker than Burgundy.
%
%   b) THE FIGURE SPACING INVARIANT IS -0.6cm, not the parent's -0.65cm.  appfig
%      closes with a RIGID \vskip 24.5pt and \figcaption opens with
%      \nointerlineskip, so the distance from the frame rule to the first
%      caption line is exactly 24.5pt - 0.6cm = 7.44pt for every figure and
%      every table in this paper, floating or inline, whatever precedes or
%      follows it on the page.  apptable closes with the same rigid skip, so a
%      table's caption sits at the same 7.44pt from its last rule.
%
%   c) CAPTIONS ARE TWO LINES, NOT THREE.  \figcaption and \tabcap each set a
%      centered italic block broken by hand onto exactly two lines of near-equal
%      width.  The paper's convention is that the two lines of one caption lie
%      within a four-character spread of each other, and every caption opens
%      with its own number, "Figure N. " or "Table N. ".
%
%   d) A NEW COVER, ADAPTED FROM THE PAPER TEMPLATE.  \trialmast sets the
%      centered cover block of new-trial-system/template-new-system: a ruled
%      title, a draft line, a DOI, the author with a green ORCID iD mark, and
%      the two notice paragraphs.  It is not the parent work's ruled panel over
%      a three-cell money ledger, because this paper's subject is a method
%      rather than three numbers.
%
% DOI RENDERING.  Every DOI in this paper sets as one accent, clickable string
% that carries its own prefix and its own closing period, exactly
% "doi:10.5281/zenodo.21887807." with the period inside the link and inside the
% color.  The mechanism is described in full at the foot of this file, under
% CLICKABLE DOIs.
%
% PROSE LINKS.  A repository link written in body text is routed to the same
% accent renderer the reference list uses, so every link the author wrote by
% hand is marked and only the machinery links, contents entries and internal
% cross-references, stay undecorated.  \ulink names that intent at the call
% site.  See PROSE LINKS at the foot of this file.
%
% SENIOR-AUTHOR FORMATTING.  RaggedRight body with even interword spacing and no
% right-margin overflow; maximal widow, orphan and broken penalties so no single
% line is stranded and no paragraph ends in a one-word or two-word line; long
% URLs break on any character; single hyphens only, no em dash and no double
% dash; the section symbol for every codified reference.  No raster images
% anywhere.
% ============================================================
\NeedsTeXFormat{LaTeX2e}
\ProvidesPackage{trialstyle}[2026/08/14 v4.6.0 ChemicalQDevice new trial system style]

